# Of or relating to [[operation]]s, especially [[military]] operations.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-22|volume=407|issue=8841|page=70|magazine=w:The Economist
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21579879-buy-out-firm-really-does-focus-operational-improvements-engineers Engineers of a different kind]
|passage=Private-equity nabobs bristle at being dubbed mere financiers.{{...}}Much of their pleading is public-relations bluster. Clever financial ploys are what have made billionaires of the industry’s veterans. “'''Operational''' improvement” in a portfolio company has often meant little more than promising colossal bonuses to sitting chief executives if they meet ambitious growth targets. That model is still prevalent today.}}
# [[functioning|Functioning]] and [[ready]] for [[use]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1977|author=w:George Lucas; Governor Tarkin|title=Star Wars
|passage=Princess Leia, before your execution, you will join me at a ceremony that will make this battle station '''operational'''. No star system will dare oppose the Emperor now.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 December 14|title=News in pictures: Class 87 soldiers on in Bulgaria|journal=RAIL|issue=972|page=26, photo caption|text=Despite somewhat faded paintwork, 87017 ''Iron Duke'' is clearly very much '''operational''', as confirmed here on September 4.}}
# [[effective|Effective]] or [[operative]].
# Determined by means of practical measures.

